Just a general comment in addition to the good advice given before: The
gates of Gehennom are not a point of no return. If you didn't feel like you
were underprepared for what now lies behind you, just go ahead. There are
only two things I can think of that make Gehennom fundamentally different:
Firetraps and the inability to pray. So get fire resistance. The monsters
appearing in Gehennom can be somewhat trickier, but with care you should
manage. You have the Eye of the Aethiopica, when you're in trouble, just
#invoke it to get out of hell free.

The real fun starts when you wake up the wizard.

